# ── C1: raw source corpora (inputs to the scripts, not the analyzer) ──
/core/c1/data/GoogleChromeExtension
core/c1/data/MaliciousBrowserExtensions/
/core/c1/data/MalCryptoExt_malicious_extensions
core/c1/data/malext_sentry and chrome_mal_ids Finalized Blocklist IDs.xlsx

# 184 MB across 103,802 files. enrich.find_local_manifest() reads it to
# recover the manifest of an extension the store has already delisted, and
# returns None when it is absent — analyzer.py already handles that and
# reports the row as unavailable, so C1 runs correctly without it. What it
# costs is enrichment coverage for delisted IDs, not function. Committing
# 103k files would make every clone, status and checkout slow permanently,
# so it is distributed alongside the repo rather than inside it.
core/c1/data/chrome-extension-manifests-dataset/

